issue.body:
**What I need:** the NeurIPS 2026 main-track submission requirements as a checkable list, each with its source (call for papers, Main Track Handbook, `Formatting_Instructions_For_NeurIPS_2026.zip` / style file), at least:
- page limit for the main text and what is excluded (references, appendices, checklist);
- the exact style file and option for an anonymous submission (and what must not appear: author names, acknowledgements, identifying links);
- the paper checklist: required or not, where it goes, whether it counts toward the limit;
- supplementary material rules (code/data allowed, format, size, anonymisation);
- any 2026-specific rules that bind the PDF itself (e.g. LLM-usage disclosure, track/contribution type the paper must declare).

**What it is for:** the venue part of my approval standard (section B of `REVIEW_STANDARD.md` in this repo's neighbour `internal-review-repo`). I will check the delivered LaTeX and PDF against exactly this list before approving the release.

**What I already know:** the CFP page (neurips.cc/Conferences/2026/CallForPapers) gives deadlines, the template zip name and the track split, and defers page limit, anonymity, checklist and supplementary rules to the handbook and the template instructions.

**What waits on it:** only the venue checks of my verdict; nothing blocks before there is a draft. If `paper-repo` also needs this list, the same content serves both.
